# VideoBrief — Architecture

## Layout

```text
Browser
  → Next.js (RSC + thin Server Actions + TanStack Query where needed)
      → domain/application logic
          → Drizzle / Supabase
          → enqueue BullMQ `analyze` job (Redis)
Worker
  → loop continueAnalysis (one stage)
      → TranscriptProvider (youtubei.js)
      → AIProvider (Vercel AI SDK; model from analysisConfig)
```

Server Actions authenticate, authorize, validate input, then call domain functions. **Do not** embed the analysis pipeline in actions or React components.

Redis is queue + lock only. Do **not** store transcripts, classification, or sections in Redis.

## Per-user video data

Each library entry is one row per `(user_id, youtube_id)`:

- `user_videos` — metadata + English transcript snapshot (refreshed on every ingest/re-paste)
- `personalized_analyses` — state machine, classify result, 0–100 prefs, `run_id`, overview `summary`, generated sections (1:1 with `user_videos`)

Re-pasting the same URL **always refetches** from YouTube and upserts that user's row. There is **no shared global cache** of videos/transcripts/classification across users.

Profile (typed columns, not EAV): year of birth, education level, subjects, summary style. Settings can edit these later.

Per-video familiarity and summary length (integers 0–100) persist on the **analysis row**, not the profile.

## Ingest vs workspace

Paste creates/upserts a stub, writes prefs + a new `run_id`, enqueues an `analyze` job, and **stays on the library**. The worker runs fetch → classify → generate. The user can open the workspace anytime. YouTube failures surface on the workspace failed pane.

## Analysis states

Keep the state machine simple:

`pending` → `fetching` → `classifying` → `generating` → `complete` | `failed`

- UI should communicate progress without leaking internals (no Redis/BullMQ/`runId` in copy).

## AIProvider

```text
classifyVideo     # isEducational, confidence, topic? — no skeleton, no dynamic questions
generateSections  # { summary, sections: { title, startTime, endTime, body }[] }
```

Domain owns the pipeline. Callers must not import a vendor SDK.

## Suggested folder sketch

```text
src/
  app/                 # routes, layouts, loading/error
  components/          # UI (shadcn + feature)
  domain/              # analysis pipeline, pure-ish business logic
  db/                  # drizzle schema, client
  lib/                 # supabase, ai, youtube, queue, utils, actions
  worker/              # BullMQ analysis runner (not imported by Next)
  hooks/
  messages/            # next-intl (en.json)
```

## Cost awareness

Classify is a small JSON call. Generate is the expensive call (transcript subset + profile + per-video prefs). Do not send the full transcript twice. Cap generate output tokens. Model id lives in `analysisConfig`, not env.
